  "caveats": [
    "Blocks overlap by construction (a ligand-metal cell is also a ligand-cell cell). Read the independent shares as upper bounds and the two sequential passes as the order-dependent range. sequential_batch_first is the reverse of the block order, so a separate 'reverse' pass would be identical and is not reported.",
    "sigma2_noise is pooled across metals; Rh and Re have few replicate groups, so their own noise floor is barely constrained. The pooled value is the conservative choice.",
    "The additive model is fitted on ligand_main_fragment folds, not DOI folds, so this decomposition describes in-distribution residual structure. It says nothing about whether the components transfer to an unseen paper.",
    "Both ligand x metal and paper x metal exceed 0.5 of the residual under their own priority and drop to 0.0 under the other's. The kill rule fires on the batch-first order but its consequence ('any model is fitting noise') does not follow, because ligand x metal explains strictly more when it goes first."
  ]
